um: vector: keep NAPI scheduled when the poll budget is exhausted

net/core/dev.c keeps a NAPI instance scheduled only if poll() returns exactly
budget without completing. Completing at work_done == budget drops the
"more work pending" signal and stalls RX under load. Same fix as
https://github.com/GlassOnTin/uml-transport (vector-napi-budget.patch).

--- a/arch/um/drivers/vector_kern.c	2026-09-26 15:41:50.567832590 +0000
+++ b/arch/um/drivers/vector_kern.c	2026-09-26 15:41:50.587950290 +0000
@@ -1180,7 +1180,7 @@
 
 	if (tx_enqueued || err > 0)
 		napi_schedule(napi);
-	if (work_done <= budget)
+	if (work_done < budget)
 		napi_complete_done(napi, work_done);
 	return work_done;
 }
